    "description": "208 AC Catelyn IX (Chapter 59) 90 House Frey The Late Lord Frey Lord Walder Frey is the aging head of House Frey and Lord of the Crossing. Nearing ninety years old, he is bald, hunched, and marked by age spots. His scrawny shoulders and long pink neck support a vulture-like head with a weasel’s face—a trait passed on to many of his descendants. His chin has receded beneath loose, dangling skin, and his runny, clouded eyes lend him a constantly irritated expression. Toothless and a&icted with gout, Walder’s mouth is rarely still, and he cannot stand without aid. Despite his infirmity, he remains active in the affairs of his house, ruling the Twins with a sharp tongue and blunt manner. Walder is notoriously irascible, self-interested, and unashamedly calculating. Age has only sharpened his impatience, but his long memory and vast brood of descendants keep his influence alive well beyond what many would expect.",
